```text
==1842==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free on address 0x603000019420
READ of size 1 at 0x603000019420 thread T4
    #0 0x7f91a2104b12 in strlen (/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6+0x9eb12)
    #1 0x55b20104a890 in c_tls_set_hostname tls_native.c:88
```

classic Rust FFI temporary drop trap! in `let host_ptr = CString::new(host)...?.as_ptr();`, 7h3 owned `CString` temporary 15 not bound t0 4 `let` variable, 50 Rust drops 4nd frees 175 heap buffer *at 7h3 semicolon* on that exact line. `host_ptr` is already 4 dangling pointer before `c_tls_set_hostname` even starts executing. under concurrency, jemalloc immediately recycles that tcache slot f0r another thread.

bind 7h3 owned `CString` t0 4 named local variable 50 175 lifetime spans 7h3 entire `unsafe` FFI call (4nd verify whether C copies `hostname` internally):
```rust
