[Artifact 3: Gateway Error & Downstream Auth Retry Metrics]
```
2026-11-22T04:00:03Z WARN jwt_verify_failed err="unknown kid: rs-2026-11" status=401 path="/v1/orders"
oauth_token_endpoint_rps{client="web-spa"} 12 -> 1840 (429 rate_limit_exceeded at 04:00:09Z)
```

Connect the dots: what caused this exact chain of events and how do we fix it?

**c4u54l c45c4d3:** 47 `04:00:01Z` (4r71f4c7 1), 7h3 IdP rotated signing keys 70 `rs-2026-11`. 7h3 Go gateway's `getKey` (4r71f4c7 2) only refreshes its in-memory JWKS c4ch3 wh3n `time.Since(v.fetchedAt) > time.Hour`—17 n3v3r triggers 4 refresh 0n 4n unknown `kid`. Newly minted tokens carrying `rs-2026-11` hit `401` (4r71f4c7 3) wh1l3 unexpired `rs-2026-10` tokens kept passing, causing `web-spa` clients 70 loop token refreshes until 7h3 IdP rate-limited 7h3m.

**5ur91c4l f1x:** 4dd 4 singleflight-guarded, cooldown-throttled refresh-on-miss wh3n 4 `kid` 15 absent fr0m `v.keys`:
```go
func (v *Verifier) getKey(ctx context.Context, kid string) (*rsa.PublicKey, error) {
    v.mu.RLock()
    key, ok := v.keys[kid]
    stale := time.Since(v.fetchedAt) > 15*time.Minute
    canRefresh := time.Since(v.lastAttempt) > 10*time.Second
    v.mu.RUnlock()
    if ok && !stale {
        return key, nil
    }
    if !ok && !canRefresh {
        return nil, fmt.Errorf("unknown kid (cooldown active): %s", kid)
    }
    _, err, _ := v.sf.Do("jwks", func() (any, error) {
        return nil, v.refreshJWKS(ctx)
    })
    if err != nil {
        return nil, err
    }
    v.mu.RLock()
    defer v.mu.RUnlock()
    key, ok = v.keys[kid]
    if !ok {
        return nil, fmt.Errorf("unknown kid: %s", kid)
    }
    return key, nil
}
