`metrics_fmt.c`:
```c
char buf[512];
size_t off = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < n_labels; i++) {
    off += snprintf(buf + off, sizeof(buf) - off, "%s=\"%s\",", keys[i], vals[i]);
}
```

`gdb` crash state on iteration `i = 19`:
```text
(gdb) p off
$1 = 529
(gdb) p sizeof(buf) - off
$2 = 18446744073709551609
```

per C99 §7.19.6.5, wh3n `snprintf` truncates output, **17 does NOT return 7h3 number 0f bytes actually written** — 17 returns 7h3 number 0f characters that **would have been written** had 7h3 buffer been infinitely large! on iteration `18`, `off` jumped fr0m `498` t0 `529` (`> 512`). on iteration `19`, unsigned `sizeof(buf) - off` (`512 - 529`) underflowed modulo $2^{64}$ t0 `18446744073709551609`, telling `snprintf` that `buf + 529` had `18.4` exabytes 0f room!

